{"id": "EUVD-2026-80486", "enisaUuid": "93c22369-0281-3f7e-a078-40cc1f0173bd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmedia: intel/ipu6: fix async notifier cleanup leak on parse error\n\nisys_notifier_init() calls v4l2_async_nf_init() and then adds fwnode\nremote subdevs in a loop with v4l2_async_nf_add_fwnode_remote(). If an\nendpoint parse or add fails partway through the loop, it jumps to\nerr_parse and returns without calling v4l2_async_nf_cleanup(), leaking\nevery v4l2_async_connection already added to the notifier's waiting\nlist.\n\nThe register-failure path just below already cleans up correctly, and\nthe caller only tears the notifier down (isys_notifier_cleanup()) once\nisys_notifier_init() has returned success. Clean up the notifier on the\nparse error path too.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:54:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd5943aedbe4d7eb46158cb35078257733ac48b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/27b7997be552ee37b3e01beacfeb4131f1bebb5f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eee6069e4e9511e814a33a75e403f7e863f70394", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/abb1f808ceab5a3275f8a6b4e37cff17f9f781c1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89886", "GHSA-3gm6-jh34-23qh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "37d0ed9e-c8ab-3800-b887-7ae4547dbbed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f50c4ca0a82003b8a542c3332fd292cf1bc355a2 <27b7997be552ee37b3e01beacfeb4131f1bebb5f"}, {"id": "49514e9b-9609-3f73-8928-710f8588c148", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "625d120e-c83b-36c0-8905-4f9e9245773d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "683c925d-9029-3bbd-97b6-eab8afb3f98c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f50c4ca0a82003b8a542c3332fd292cf1bc355a2 <abb1f808ceab5a3275f8a6b4e37cff17f9f781c1"}, {"id": "d1e44b6f-7bb4-3aaa-845e-bc6976b2a36d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d4019b69-2653-3f40-90d9-2d914a508d90", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "db865389-d320-3ed8-a93d-f282df7a44fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "eddcb4c9-2174-34c0-a6c8-d8deb6cdeb0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "eea0a7a4-4566-3972-8a08-f511beb5057a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f50c4ca0a82003b8a542c3332fd292cf1bc355a2 <eee6069e4e9511e814a33a75e403f7e863f70394"}, {"id": "f7a9d53a-deb6-32fe-8ef2-9a433e1c6fb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f50c4ca0a82003b8a542c3332fd292cf1bc355a2 <dd5943aedbe4d7eb46158cb35078257733ac48b6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8de340f3-9e8a-35c2-a2d3-eaa3b2a12767", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}